B4.3.47 RMI_VDEV_ABORT command
               Abort device communication associated with a VDEV.
               B4.3.47.1 Interface
               B4.3.47.1.1   Input values
        Name                 Register    Bits        Type                                  Description
        fid                  X0          63:0        UInt64                                FID, value 0xC4000185
        vdev_ptr             X1          63:0        Address                               PA of the VDEV
               B4.3.47.1.2   Context
               The RMI_VDEV_ABORT command operates on the following context.
        Name                 Type                       Value                                      Before   Description
        vdev                 RmmVdev                    VdevAt(vdev_ptr)                           false    VDEV
               B4.3.47.1.3   Output values
        Name                 Register    Bits        Type                                  Description
        result               X0          63:0        RmiCommandReturnCode                  Command return status
               B4.3.47.2 Failure conditions
  ID                          Condition
  da_supp                     pre: ImplFeatures().feat_da != FEATURE_TRUE
                              post: ResultEqual(result, RMI_ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED)
  vdev_align                  pre: !AddrIsGranuleAligned(vdev_ptr)
                              post: ResultEqual(result, RMI_ERROR_INPUT)
  vdev_bound                  pre: !PaIsDelegable(vdev_ptr)
                              post: ResultEqual(result, RMI_ERROR_INPUT)
  vdev_gran_state             pre: GranuleAt(vdev_ptr).state != VDEV
                              post: ResultEqual(result, RMI_ERROR_INPUT)
  comm_state                  pre: vdev.comm_state == DEV_COMM_IDLE
                              post: ResultEqual(result, RMI_ERROR_DEVICE)
             B4.3.47.2.1   Failure condition ordering
             [da_supp] < [vdev_align, vdev_bound, vdev_gran_state]
             [vdev_gran_state] < [comm_state]
                                                            da_supp
                                                 RMI_ERROR_NOT _SUPPORT ED
                           vdev_bound                     vdev_align                     vdev_gran_state
                                                                                                   RMI_ERROR_INPUT
                                                                                            RMI_ERROR_DEVICE
             B4.3.47.3 Success conditions
  ID                        Condition
  state                     post: vdev.vdev_state == VDEV_ERROR
  comm_state                post: vdev.comm_state == DEV_COMM_IDLE
             B4.3.47.4 Footprint
    ID                        Value
    state                     vdev.vdev_state
    comm_state                vdev.comm_state

